---
/**
 * /preview-index — the homepage, at a URL you can open before launch.
 *
 * The site root 302s to /coming-soon until the studio opens (see
 * src/pages/index.astro), so the homepage has no address of its own. This is
 * that address.
 *
 * It RENDERS /early-access rather than copying it. That page is the homepage:
 * "the full editorial homepage layout, as it will read once open" — the
 * original homepage's content rebuilt on the version-H system, with the
 * booking CTAs already pointed at the waitlist while booking is closed. A
 * second copy of 500 lines would drift from it within a week; a rewrite keeps
 * this URL showing whatever that page says today.
 *
 * The URL in the address bar stays /preview-index (a rewrite, not a redirect).
 * The page it renders carries its own `noindex`, and robots.txt disallows this
 * path too — an unlaunched homepage must not compete with /coming-soon for the
 * brand's own name.
 *
 * When the studio opens, this page's content belongs at `/` and this route can
 * go with the redirect in src/pages/index.astro.
 */
export const prerender = false;

return Astro.rewrite("/early-access");
---
